                "event": "Coastal Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Wakefield VA",
                "headline": "Coastal Flood Warning issued November 25 at 2:18PM EST until November 26 at 3:00PM EST by NWS Wakefield VA",
                "description": "* WHAT...2 to 3 feet of inundation above ground level expected in low-\nlying areas near shorelines and tidal waterways.\n\n* WHERE...Chesapeake and Suffolk, and Hampton/Poquoson, Norfolk\nand Portsmouth Counties.\n\n* WHEN...Until 3 PM EST Thursday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Major flooding may cause extensive inundation and\nflooding of numerous roads and buildings resulting in a\nsignificant threat to property and life. Water will be 2 to 3\nfeet or more above ground level in some areas. Flooding may\nextend inland from the waterfront and shoreline flooding\nhomes, businesses and isolating some neighborhoods. Numerous\nroads may become impassable under several feet of water and\ncars submerged.",
                "instruction": "Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone property. If\ntravel is required, do not drive around barricades or through\nwater of unknown depth.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
