                "headline": "High Wind Warning issued November 25 at 12:01PM EST until November 26 at 1:00PM EST by NWS Wakefield VA",
                "description": "* WHAT...East winds 30 to 40 mph with gusts up to 60 mph expected.\n\n* WHERE...Chesapeake and Suffolk, and Isle of Wight and Surry\nCounties.\n\n* WHEN...From 7 PM this evening to 1 PM EST Thursday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Damaging winds will blow down trees and power lines.\nWidespread power outages are expected. Travel will be difficult,\nespecially for high profile vehicles.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...The strongest winds are expected between 2 AM\nand 9 AM EST Thursday.",
                "instruction": "People are urged to secure loose objects that could be blown around\nor damaged by the wind.",
                "response": "Prepare",
